s counted in stock at each holder.", "kept_in": [{"component": "stock", "field": "clay"}]}, {"resource_id": "leads", "says": "Pencil leads are counted in stock at each holder.", "kept_in": [{"component": "stock", "field": "leads"}]}, {"resource_id": "paint", "says": "Paint is counted in stock at each holder.", "kept_in": [{"component": "stock", "field": "paint"}]}, {"resource_id": "erasers", "says": "Erasers are counted in stock at each holder.", "kept_in": [{"component": "stock", "field": "erasers"}]}, {"resource_id": "ferrules", "says": "Brass ferrules are counted in stock at each holder.", "kept_in": [{"component": "stock", "field": "ferrules"}]}, {"resource_id": "pencils", "says": "Pencils are counted in stock at each holder.", "kept_in": [{"component": "stock", "field": "pencils"}, {"component": "shipment", "field": "pencils_in_transit"}]}, {"resource_id": "boxes", "says": "Packing boxes are counted in stock at each holder.", "kept_in": [{"component": "stock", "field": "boxes"}]}], "laws": [{"law_id": "logs-accounting", "says": "The total number of logs changes only when cedar is cut or logs are sawn into slats.", "resource": "logs", "may_change_by": ["cut-cedar", "saw-slats"]}, {"law_id": "slats-accounting", "says": "The total number of slats changes only when logs are sawn or slats are assembled into pencils.", "resource": "slats", "may_change_by": ["saw-slats", "assemble-pencils"]}, {"law_id": "graphite-accounting", "says": "The total amount of graphite changes only when it is mined or mixed into leads.", "resource": "graphite", "may_change_by": ["mine-graphite", "make-leads"]}, {"law_id": "clay-accounting", "says": "The total amount of clay changes only when it is mixed into leads.", "resource": "clay", "may_change_by": ["make-leads"]}, {"law_id": "leads-accounting", "says": "The total number of leads changes only when leads are made or assembled into pencils.", "resource": "leads", "may_change_by": ["make-leads", "assemble-pencils"]}, {"law_id": "pencils-accounting", "says": "The total number of pencils changes only when pencils are assembled or packed into boxes.", "resource": "pencils", "may_change_by": ["assemble-pencils", "pack-boxes"]}, {"law_id": "boxes-accounting", "says": "The total number of boxes changes only when boxes are packed or replenished.", "resource": "boxes", "may_change_by": ["pack-boxes", "restock-boxes"]}]}", "role": "assistant"}, {"content": "Rules were written for that structure and test-run, and this is what happened: A separate check read your rules against the description and the laws and found: nothing in the rules: There is no rule or process for a delivery to arrive, so pencils placed in transit never actually reach the shops. (the description says: "deliver the boxes to shops") nothing in the rules: There are no rules to acquire more clay, paint, erasers, or ferrules, so the supply chain will permanently halt once the starting stocks are consumed. (the description says: "keeps running") Fix each of these. This is an ongoing world. A deterministic dry run of your previous mechanics gave: terminal null, 0 processes, active in the last rounds: True (over 24 rounds). Set terminal to null and add processes so state keeps changing and the actors keep having useful actions in every round indefinitely: needs and resources must keep cycling (for example hunger rises, eating lowers it, food regrows), never just run down to a stop. In the 24-round test these actors stopped being able to do anything (or never could): shops-business (refused: it was never offered an action). Every actor role must be able to act regularly: make sure some actor's action brings what each one's action needs to where it is checked (for example, if a carrier must hold goods before delivering, give another actor an action that loads goods onto the carrier, or let the carrier pick them up itself). A process may renew raw materials at their source or bring new demand, but never supply what an action makes or move goods between places. In the 24-round test these moves were never possible for anyone: sell-pencils (nothing it applies to ever existed, or no actor ever held what it needs). For each, make sure some other action produces what its checks need (for example, if goods must be at the next stop before they can move on, give someone an action that brings them there). These moves use up a good where it never arrives, so they can never happen: sell-pencils needs pencils at shops-business, which starts with none and nothing ever gives it any. Give the holder a source: the step that makes or carries the good must add it there (a delivery that counts down must add the goods to the receiver when it ends). Rules can only change the actor and the entities its fields name, and cannot add actions or fields. Return a corrected structure (JSON object only) whose actions and fields let every step and every actor happen, keeping what already worked. Keep the world's resources and laws, updated for every action you add, rename or change: a move that makes or uses up a resource belongs in that law's may_change_by, and a trade its pairing law names must still exist.", "role": "user"}], "prompt_ref": null, "control": {"timeout": 0, "num_retries": 1, "reasoning_effort": "low", "api_base": null, "base_delay": 1.0, "max_delay": 30.0, "retry_on": null, "fallback_models": null, "manual_fallback": null, "execution_mode": "text", "structured_output_mode": null, "structured_contract_ref": null, "retry_policy": {"max_retries": 1, "base_delay": 1.0, "max_delay": 30.0, "retry_on": null, "on_retry": null, "backoff": null, "should_retry": null}, "cache_policy": {"mode": "disabled"}, "max_budget": 0.2}, "kwargs": {"max_tokens": 16000, "model_policy": "enforce_allowlist"}, "response_model_fqn": null, "response_model_schema": null}, "replay": {"unsupported_keys": []}}

